{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1361700-starting-an-adventure-advice","id":1361700,"title":"Starting an adventure, advice?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-18T03:08:10-08:00","id":1361700,"title":"Starting an adventure, advice?","content":"Hi, i'm intending to run Aeon at some point. I've been familiar with the setting on and off since it initially appeared way back when. However I've never run it, nor the Storypath system.<br /> <br /> What I want to do is open with a particular scene, mainly to introduce the story and teach some rules. This scene will come before actual character creation and so won't use whoever the players go on to create. In this scene an Aberant appears approaching earth orbit intending to attack. The players will be the defence force sent to intercept and so the battle will be the scene in question.<br /> <br /> Are there any issues I ought be aware of before running this? The mass vehicle combat rules seem incredibly abstract (and hopefully simple)?<br /> <br /> Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25906-ghost-whistler","name":"ghost whistler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25906_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-18T04:31:05-08:00","id":1361704,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t see any issues with this idea, actually it\u2019s a great way to introduce both the setting and the rule system.<br /> <br /> The mass vehicle combat rules are very abstract, as most of the mass combat rules are, but it can be very interesting if you put the players to do the turning points. You get all the scale of an aberrant fighting a bunch of heavy weaponed ships, without the need of controlling the entire army or be a zergling in a Zerg rush. The issue is what are going to be the turning points.<br /> <br /> Another option is using few ships but heavy ones, with the players controlling the entire ships, like a frigate and a few patrols. You don\u2019t need even a character to play like this. I mean, you need characters, the ships, but they can be built as antagonists much simpler to build and yet very effective in game.<br /> <br /> Anyway, good luck with your game!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-18T05:14:21-08:00","id":1361715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1361700-starting-an-adventure-advice?p=1361704#post1361704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t see any issues with this idea, actually it\u2019s a great way to introduce both the setting and the rule system.<br /> <br /> The mass vehicle combat rules are very abstract, as most of the mass combat rules are, but it can be very interesting if you put the players to do the turning points. You get all the scale of an aberrant fighting a bunch of heavy weaponed ships, without the need of controlling the entire army or be a zergling in a Zerg rush. The issue is what are going to be the turning points.<br /> <br /> Another option is using few ships but heavy ones, with the players controlling the entire ships, like a frigate and a few patrols. You don\u2019t need even a character to play like this. I mean, you need characters, the ships, but they can be built as antagonists much simpler to build and yet very effective in game.<br /> <br /> Anyway, good luck with your game!</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. I too will eb learning the rules, which is why I was asking.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how much stuff the players should have. Do they need to be an entire armada of starship like at Wolf 359 in Star Trek? Could they be VARG pilots? There will be thre players and I'm not keen on running loads of NPC's if that's what it takes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25906-ghost-whistler","name":"ghost whistler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25906_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-18T05:30:06-08:00","id":1361716,"title":"","content":"Well... the more you give them, more challenging it will be to deal with the rules. VARGs for example are quite complex with all the scale and special properties. If you start small it will be easier, and that\u2019s why I suggested the idea of each player handle an entire ship, as it is simpler than a complete character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-18T08:29:00-08:00","id":1361736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1361700-starting-an-adventure-advice?p=1361716#post1361716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well... the more you give them, more challenging it will be to deal with the rules. VARGs for example are quite complex with all the scale and special properties. If you start small it will be easier, and that\u2019s why I suggested the idea of each player handle an entire ship, as it is simpler than a complete character.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What ships would you suggest? Wouldn't they be just as complex for the same reasons?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25906-ghost-whistler","name":"ghost whistler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25906_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-18T11:20:50-08:00","id":1361771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ghost whistler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1361700-starting-an-adventure-advice?p=1361736#post1361736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> What ships would you suggest? Wouldn't they be just as complex for the same reasons?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would go for a Frigate and 2 Patrols. Give me some time and I give you the tags and stats you need.<br /> <br /> the reason why they can be less complicated is that they are operated by an entire troop, so the individuals are matter is statistics. Instead of a complete character you can work with Primary, Secondary and desperation dice pools, some edges and the proper Starship tags.<br /> <br /> You will get the general combat rules (momentum, injuries, stunts, etc) without all the details you may need to create a entire character, no need for discussing the concepts behind the skill tricks, specialities, skill picking, attribute picking, and things like that until you have your own character with the stats you choose.<br /> <br /> you also get some of the most infamous and one of the greatest ideas in Storypath, that is the Scale. You may need it later and dealing with it on a less complex environment is better to get the concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-18T12:41:05-08:00","id":1361781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1361700-starting-an-adventure-advice?p=1361771#post1361771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would go for a Frigate and 2 Patrols. Give me some time and I give you the tags and stats you need.<br /> <br /> the reason why they can be less complicated is that they are operated by an entire troop, so the individuals are matter is statistics. Instead of a complete character you can work with Primary, Secondary and desperation dice pools, some edges and the proper Starship tags.<br /> <br /> You will get the general combat rules (momentum, injuries, stunts, etc) without all the details you may need to create a entire character, no need for discussing the concepts behind the skill tricks, specialities, skill picking, attribute picking, and things like that until you have your own character with the stats you choose.<br /> <br /> you also get some of the most infamous and one of the greatest ideas in Storypath, that is the Scale. You may need it later and dealing with it on a less complex environment is better to get the concept.</div> </div> </div> </div> thanks.again!<br /> <br /> So you're saying i can just abstract character stats? That certainly would be helpful for learning<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25906-ghost-whistler","name":"ghost whistler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25906_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-18T14:38:47-08:00","id":1361789,"title":"","content":"For the Frigate use the tags Armor 2, Cargo 2, Computer 0, Crew \u22122, Hybrid 2, Massive 2, Military 1, Psi \u22121, Thrusters 2 and for the patrol the tags Armor 2, Cargo 1, Computer 0, Crew \u22121, Hybrid 2, Massive 1, Military 1, Psi \u22121, Thrusters 3. You will need to pick some weapons, just pick from the character options and consider them the proper size.<br /> <br /> You will deal with the speed, size and power scales, so it\u2019s a nice way to start.<br /> <br /> What I am suggesting for character stats is to use of Antagonist stats as crew stats to operate the ships, check Trinity Core page 137, give them Moderate threat stats and they would be ready to play. They are easy to build and easy to play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-19T03:21:02-08:00","id":1361881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1361700-starting-an-adventure-advice?p=1361789#post1361789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the Frigate use the tags Armor 2, Cargo 2, Computer 0, Crew \u22122, Hybrid 2, Massive 2, Military 1, Psi \u22121, Thrusters 2 and for the patrol the tags Armor 2, Cargo 1, Computer 0, Crew \u22121, Hybrid 2, Massive 1, Military 1, Psi \u22121, Thrusters 3. You will need to pick some weapons, just pick from the character options and consider them the proper size.<br /> <br /> You will deal with the speed, size and power scales, so it\u2019s a nice way to start.<br /> <br /> What I am suggesting for character stats is to use of Antagonist stats as crew stats to operate the ships, check Trinity Core page 137, give them Moderate threat stats and they would be ready to play. They are easy to build and easy to play.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, but what sort of aberrant could match that frigate? What stats should I use there?<br /> <br /> If one player's in command of that frigate, what do the rest do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25906-ghost-whistler","name":"ghost whistler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25906_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-19T03:41:53-08:00","id":1361885,"title":"","content":"A Terat can destroy the frigate if you play right, as they can have a lot of scale. Put some speed scale to match the ships and power and durability to be able to hold the fire of the patrol ship except for a really good shot.<br /> <br /> another option is to have a few deviants and a large number of sub Aberrants. The sub-Aberrants die like flys, but there are lots of them, while the deviants can damage the ships with some difficulty.<br /> <br /> Each player command one of the ships, 1 commands the big but slow, and the other 2 commands the faster but lighter ships.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-19T07:31:24-08:00","id":1361898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1361700-starting-an-adventure-advice?p=1361885#post1361885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Terat can destroy the frigate if you play right, as they can have a lot of scale. Put some speed scale to match the ships and power and durability to be able to hold the fire of the patrol ship except for a really good shot.<br /> <br /> another option is to have a few deviants and a large number of sub Aberrants. The sub-Aberrants die like flys, but there are lots of them, while the deviants can damage the ships with some difficulty.<br /> <br /> Each player command one of the ships, 1 commands the big but slow, and the other 2 commands the faster but lighter ships.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks again, My concern would be that as commanders of ships they don't get to interact as much. That's why I oriented to VARGS initially. Plus i'd rather not have to deal with large crews. Commanding ships in an unfamiliar game might be a tall order.<br /> <br /> Hard to guage the kind of threat, Terat's might be a bit too big. Scale 4 is pretty huge!<br /> <br /> Thanks for your help","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25906-ghost-whistler","name":"ghost whistler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25906_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-19T12:15:39-08:00","id":1361949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ghost whistler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1361700-starting-an-adventure-advice?p=1361898#post1361898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Thanks again, My concern would be that as commanders of ships they don't get to interact as much. That's why I oriented to VARGS initially. Plus i'd rather not have to deal with large crews. Commanding ships in an unfamiliar game might be a tall order.<br /> <br /> Hard to guage the kind of threat, Terat's might be a bit too big. Scale 4 is pretty huge!<br /> <br /> Thanks for your help</div> </div> </div> </div>What is the nature/plot of your adventure and the importance of this scene? I'm assuming that the players' characters arent going to be the actual commanders of these ships in your game. Are their characters on the ships? Will the Aberrant likely get away and be their nemesis later (or perhaps the attack is cover to allow a different Aberrant to get to Earth)? Something completely different? It's a pretty cool scene and I'm curious as to how it relates to your adventure as a whole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-19T12:33:04-08:00","id":1361953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1361700-starting-an-adventure-advice?p=1361949#post1361949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What is the nature/plot of your adventure and the importance of this scene? I'm assuming that the players' characters arent going to be the actual commanders of these ships in your game. Are their characters on the ships? Will the Aberrant likely get away and be their nemesis later (or perhaps the attack is cover to allow a different Aberrant to get to Earth)? Something completely different? It's a pretty cool scene and I'm curious as to how it relates to your adventure as a whole.</div> </div> </div> </div>Twofold:<br /> To setup the scenario. The basis of which is that an Aberrant attack is foiled and the Aberrant gets shipped to a secret research facility targeted by a sympathetic cult. They are working for a corporation that wants to use aberrant dna for profit. <br /> Secondly, as an intro to the game and system. Then we roll up characters. It's not meant to be a long scene at all. I don't think their actual characters will be present since I don't know what characters they will create.<br /> <br /> I just need to figure out how to make it interesting for the players, if we go with the commanding ships idea. That might be puting a bit too much info their way (partly why I igured VARGS might be better). The Aberrant is going to die, but there's no need for the characters to survive <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25906-ghost-whistler","name":"ghost whistler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25906_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}